    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm a freelance designer and i'm trying to clean up my quickbooks for the year. i just bought a really expensive ergonomic chair for my home studio setup. do i categorize that as a business expense or is it a personal draw? i'm a bit confused about how the irs views home office equipment.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For a freelance designer, that ergonomic chair is almost certainly a business expense, provided you can tie it directly to your work. It's a necessary piece of equipment for your home office setup, which the IRS generally allows you to deduct if you meet the home office requirements. You should categorize it under \"Office Supplies\" or \"Equipment\" in QuickBooks. If you're unsure about the exact deduction method, consulting a tax professional is always the safest bet.",
