      "content": "The best defense against an audit is meticulous record-keeping, which is exactly what you're trying to do! You should aim to keep digital copies of *every single receipt* for every expense, whether it's the chair or a cup of coffee. Furthermore, try to reconcile your bank and credit card statements with QuickBooks every single month.\n\nIf your books are tidy, the IRS auditor will find things much easier to follow, and they are far less likely to nitpick over minor discrepancies. A clean system is your best shield against any surprise scrutiny.",
